      "status": "fixed",
      "status_notes": "PSF-2019-16 (bpo-39073): email.headerregistry.Address accepted CR and LF characters in its display name, username, domain and addr_spec arguments, allowing email header injection. Fixed upstream in 2020 by https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/614f17211c5fc0e5b828be1d3320661d1038fe8f (https://bugs.python.org/issue39073, https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PSF-2019-16); the advisory lists no CPython 3.14 release as affected, and the fix commit is in every CPython 3.14 release. Checked Address.__init__() in Lib/email/headerregistry.py (it raises ValueError when any part contains CR or LF) in every published build of the DHI Alpine 3.23 python-3.14 package, 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.10-r4, on x86_64 and aarch64: every build has the fixed code. Every published build has the fix, so the range ends at the lowest published build, 3.14.3-r0."
